A||||2||la9||Replacing Fuel Lines||||1||
Z||000000||la9||04-06-2001||08:54 AM||||I'm about to change my fuel pump and my fuel lines are pretty rusted so I'd like to replace them. I was wondering if anyone has changed their fuel lines lately and what they used as replacements.<P>Peace||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||04-06-2001||11:18 AM||||Are they rusted inside or outside? If it is outside try some wool  sponge on them (00 or 000). I did that to the break line in the front compartment and they look like new now.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-06-2001||08:23 PM||||The steel lines can be replaced. not a big deal if you have the bending tool(s).<P>Make sure any rubber line you use is the high pressure stuff. Especially if it's a V6. Those run 40-50PSI from the pump to the rail.||||reg||1
